What Is an IP Camera?
An IP camera, also known as an Internet Protocol camera, is a digital surveillance camera that transmits video and other data over a network. Unlike traditional analog CCTV cameras, IP cameras can connect to a local network and, when properly configured, allow authorized users to view live footage remotely through a smartphone, computer, or tablet.
IP cameras are available in various models, including indoor cameras, outdoor cameras, dome cameras, bullet cameras, PTZ (pan-tilt-zoom) cameras, and high-resolution cameras. The best option depends on your property's layout, lighting conditions, monitoring requirements, and security objectives.
